// Le Douzième Coup · chapter 7, the one who stays, first half (act II, five days before the sixtieth Grand Midi).
// Five leagues from the foot of Roquebise to the Thiorne. Two leagues of the land of the Leap (a night carter), the
// rope of the year 595 and its guard post taken over a game of cards (`r:sait_acceleration`: the daily advance of the
// edge, in paces, doubled for years before the Leap), then three leagues that the Dormante took at a walk between
// 575 and 595, one season after another: twenty winters before noon (the snow that keeps the dew: sand), a farm
// closed with a note under the pot, a Slow one wheeling home a clock, a dispatch rider (`r:estafette_vu`). At the
// river held in flood since the night of 575, the camp of the Mastery of Sands around the fourteenth stone: the main
// gate (the brigadier's coat and the word), the kitchens of big Mahaut (`r:mahaut_amie` if Gontran was sent home,
// `r:mahaut_dette` if he was stripped), or the edge of the held water. The morning ends with a hole to dig under the
// nose of forty guards (M07).
